// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// CHECKLIST — seed data
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// The `checklist` list below seeds the checklist app on first load. Once the
// user starts checking things off, the app keeps its own copy in localStorage
// (key "rathjiGeneratorChecklist") — edits here only matter for brand-new
// visitors. Each item is plain text like "name (N views) (priv)"; the app
// parses the view count and privacy marker into little badges.

// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// FEATURE TODO — improvements planned for this app (so they don't get lost)
// Mark ✅ as done when shipped.
//   1. ✅ Undo — every mutating action (marking done, deleting, clearing,
//      reset) shows a toast with an "Undo" button.
//   2. ✅ Reorder — drag-and-drop (or ↑/↓ buttons) for items and sections.
//   3. ✅ Search/filter — toolbar search box filtering items across all sections.
//   4. ✅ Priorities & tags — per-item priority (high/med/low) or color tags,
//      with sort-by-priority.
//   5. ✅ Due dates + overdue flags — optional date per item, red "overdue"
//      styling, "Sort by due date".
//   6. ✅ Recurring items — items that reset to unchecked daily/weekly/monthly.
//   7. ✅ Cloud sync — back up the checklist to an editable file URL so it
//      follows the user across devices (auto-restore optional).
//   8. ✅ Share by URL — encode the checklist into a ?share= link for one-click
//      sharing/importing.
//   9. ✅ Bulk actions — "check all / uncheck all / clear done" per section plus
//      keyboard shortcuts (press ? to see them).
//  10. ✅ Stats & streaks — completion history per day/section, streak counters,
//      a small 14-day chart, and a confetti burst when a section hits 100%.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

uploadPlugin = {import:upload-plugin}

$meta
  title = Checklist
  description = A simple, organized checklist — sections, completed tracking, local storage, and JSON/Markdown import & export.
  tags = checklist, todo, productivity, local storage, organization
  header
    mode = minimal

checklist
  section
    name = Example: Groceries
    items
      Milk (med) (due 2026-08-28)
      Bread
      Eggs (high) (due 2026-08-20)
      Coffee beans (low)
  section
    name = Example: Weekend
    items
      Book a campsite (high) (due 2026-08-20)
      Pack tent & sleeping bags
      Buy marshmallows (low)
      Feed the cat (daily)
